					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/adminbright" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(224440); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=224440&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609536278" alt="AdminBright" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=224440)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/adminbright" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(224440); return false;" >AdminBright</a></span> <span class="odate time_1323976212 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Dec 2011 19:10</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1329009">
									

<p>As long as hes on a body, the core personality in the amulet is in charge, even past thirty days. It's just that, if it goes past thirty days, and he comes off, it's a new Bright, one who grows and changes differently from the core personality inside the amulet.</p>
<p>Another of my head canony bits is that 963, while it has no psychic lure, tends to end up in places where it can be picked up, if left unused. Lock it up in a vault, and, during the next Keter outbreak, or insurgency attack, it'll end up being blown out of said vault, and right into a spot where someone who doesn't know what it is will pick it up.</p>

							</div>

